Virtual laboratory and quantitative exercises — ChemCollective (@gc-collective: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gc-sources) { r_246CB9EYQ2A1SQFHPV15F4Q4WT
ChemCollective. [Official virtual-laboratory stockroom, introduction, and support](https://chemcollective.org/vlab).

Use the external virtual laboratory for explicitly modelled solution, stoichiometry, and equilibrium exercises. Read its introduction and activity assumptions, predict a result, perform a virtual study, and compare with independent arithmetic. Keep a record of chosen quantities, model assumptions, activity/version, and any discrepancy. A virtual transfer does not establish practical competence with actual glassware or chemicals.

The official page recommends a current browser and states Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivs 3.0 for the site/content, with actual component terms preserved. This supports authorized external consultation; adaptation or redistribution needs attention to those conditions. The page and support links were checked on 29 October 2026; the interactive application itself was not represented as executed. No software, dataset, or media is embedded in this repository.

**Return:** [General chemistry sources — books, courses, data, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_37CHT3QSMD33JDMXE59S6M2ME3).
